  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL. Confirm 135, 136, 138 and 139 have merged; re-read their outcomes (the CallerPrincipal rights semantics and the shared core's signature may have changed). Verify ADR-008's exact file name under .claude/adr/.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Schema (prescriptive)">(a) Author the dry-run-default column script per the AP-13 constraint, and run it with -DryRun only; record the output. (b) STOP for the OPERATOR to run it for real on spaarkedev1. (c) Read the column back and assert its prefix, target and solution membership; record the metadata in notes. (d) Update the SpaarkeCore entity-schema.md for sprk_externalrecordaccess. Code that binds the new lookup must not merge before (c) passes.</step>
    <step order="2">Extend the shared grant core to accept a contact grantor (writes the new lookup, leaves sprk_grantedby empty) and a no-downgrade / no-expiry-shortening mode used only by the contact route. /grant and /invite-and-grant behaviour must not change.</step>
    <step order="3">Routes on the /api/v1/external group (names are the executor's, shape is binding): POST grant (root type + id, grantee email or contact id, level, optional expiry, optional first/last name for the CIAM new-person branch); GET the grants the caller issued on a root; POST revoke of one issued grant. Attach ContactGrantorFilter to all three.</step>
    <step order="4">ContactGrantorFilter: contact principal only; grantor level ≥ Collaborate on the root; grantor has ≥1 active organization. Handler: resolve the grantee strictly within the grantor's organizations (by contact id, or by email among active org members — ambiguous match refused 409 `sdap.access.contact_grant.grantee_ambiguous`); self-grant 400; deny-list 422; then the shared core (policy → cap → upsert).</step>
    <step order="5">New-person branch (email matches no member of the grantor's organizations): see escalation trigger 1 — implement only the owner-confirmed rule. Workforce-plane grantors never reach this branch.</step>
    <step order="6">Revoke: issued-by-caller check, grantor level ≥ Collaborate on the root, deactivate via ExternalGrantLifecycle, cache invalidation as the core does; every failure returns a message.</step>
    <step order="7">External SPA: canInvite = Collaborate or Full Access; the dialog offers only levels ≤ the caller's level, posts to the new route, renders server refusal messages verbatim, and reports narrowing; the Contacts tab lists the caller's issued grants with Revoke; remove or repoint the dead `/api/v1/external-access/*` calls in bff-client.ts and the mock service.</step>
    <step order="8">Manage Access (AccessGrantModal): Current Access rows for contact-issued grants show "granted by {contact}"; systemusers can still revoke them with the existing /revoke.
- Task 066 (open) rebases Current Access onto task 064's record-access report, with provenance per row. If 064/066 have merged, carry the contact grantor as a field of the report DTO and render it in 066's row model.
- If they have not, add it to the current row model (grant list read) and record in notes that 064/066 must carry it. The main session amends 066 accordingly.
- Do not build a second provenance mechanism.</step>
    <step order="9">Tests (scope = acceptance criteria): ContactGrantAuthorizationTests (new, tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/, KEEP path) for every allow/deny rule; RouteAuthorizationGuardTests registration.</step>
    <step order="10">Docs: EXTERNAL-ACCESS-SPA-GUIDE.md, external-access-spa-architecture.md, uac-access-control.md — contact-side granting rules, routes, audit column, revoke semantics.</step>
    <step order="11">Build + suites; external-spa `npm run build` + `npm run lint`; publish size + CVE per constraints.</step>
    <step order="12" name="Manual live gate">Deploy BFF (bff-deploy) and the external SPA (power-page-deploy or its current deployment skill) to dev; run the live gate below; record in notes/task-140-contact-side-grant.md.</step>
    <step order="13">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`. Document deviations in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>1. NEW-PERSON INVITES (open owner question — Q2 covered "contacts of their own organization" but not people who are not yet contacts). Before implementing the branch where the email matches no existing member of the grantor's organizations, STOP and obtain the owner's rule.
- This question is bound to trigger 6. Making a new person "a contact of the grantor's organization" means CREATING a `sprk_contactorganization` membership, and trigger 6 recommends that contacts may NOT create memberships.
- Recommended default: REFUSE the new-person branch on this route with 422 `sdap.access.contact_grant.grantee_not_in_organization` and a message ("{email} is not yet a member of your organization in this system; ask the record's team to add them").
- Alternative, only if the owner answers YES to trigger 6: allow it on the CIAM plane only, when the email's domain equals the grantor organization's `sprk_organization.sprk_domain` (non-empty). It creates the contact plus an active membership and onboards via ProvisionAsync, knowingly widening every organization-wide grant to that organization.
- The existing-member branch ships regardless.</trigger>
    <trigger>2. GRANTOR-LEVEL SOURCE ON STANDARD RECORDS (open owner question). The owner said "a contact with Collaborate or Full Access" without saying whether access derived from an ORGANIZATION grant or a STANDING grant counts.
- Recommendation, implemented by default: the caller's effective post-veto level. On Secure/Limited that is necessarily the direct grant; on Standard it includes organization and standing access, because the owner's rule is about the level a contact HOLDS.
- If the owner answers "direct grants only", STOP and switch the filter to the direct level rather than improvising.</trigger>
    <trigger>3. GRANT LIFETIME AND OWNERSHIP VS GRANTOR (open owner question). Three questions:
- (i) May a contact-issued grant carry an expiry later than the grantor's own grant?
- (ii) Does it survive the grantor losing access?
- (iii) May a contact raise a colleague's EXISTING grant that someone else issued? This task refuses it with managed_elsewhere.
Recommendation:
- (i) Cap the issued expiry at the grantor's own effective expiry when the grantor's level rests on a dated grant, so a grantor cannot hand out time they do not hold (the time analogue of owner Q1).
- (ii) No automatic cascade. Issued rows stand on their own, carry the contact-grantor column, and are visible and revocable in Manage Access.
- (iii) Keep the refusal.
This task implements (ii) and (iii) as recommended and the binding +90 default. For (i), STOP and ask before shipping. Whatever the owner decides is added HERE, not in a follow-up.</trigger>
    <trigger>4a. If task 141 (oid binding) or task 013 (no-hijack) has not merged, STOP before enabling the workforce contact-only grantor path. Do not ship it by relying on "dev has no such principals" (contact.azureactivedirectoryobjectid is absent in dev, so every Type-2 employee is 403 there today). The hijack path exists wherever that column exists but is empty.</trigger>
    <trigger>4. If tasks 135/136 have not delivered CIAM-plane veto parity and rights-based gates, STOP: without them a CIAM contact's level on a Restricted or Secure root can be wrong, and this route would mint access from that wrong level.</trigger>
    <trigger>5. If adr-check flags the CIAM-reachable access-minting route against ADR-028 (plane rules) or ADR-008, surface it per CLAUDE.md §6.5 as path A/B/C with this POML's rationale — do not move the route onto the workforce-only management group. (ADR-028 A3 already requires plane-agnostic routes on the one ExternalCollaboration group and forbids a second workforce entry point, so this placement is expected to be path C, comply.)</trigger>
    <trigger>6. ORGANIZATION MEMBERSHIPS (open owner question, raised 2026-09-30 by the orchestrator): may an external contact create or alter ORGANIZATION MEMBERSHIPS (`sprk_contactorganization`), for example to add a colleague to their firm?
- Recommendation: NO.
- A membership is not a grant on one record. It silently widens EVERY organization-wide grant made to that organization, on every record, and also feeds org-expansion and the deny-list's organization match. That would let one contact multiply access far beyond "at or below their own level on this record" (owner Q1/Q2).
- Membership stays an internal (systemuser / admin) action.
- This task implements the recommendation: no route or code path here writes `sprk_contactorganization` (asserted). If the owner answers YES, STOP and re-scope with trigger 1's alternative; do not add membership writes silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Grant writes: GrantExternalAccessEndpoint /grant and InviteAndGrantExternalUserEndpoint /invite-and-grant (Api/ExternalAccess/, mapped on the management group at ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:123-155). Contact-principal writes: ExternalProjectDataEndpoints (todos/documents/events, ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:92) — no grant route (grep `MapPost` in ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs → only todos, documents, events). Audit column: sprk_externalrecordaccess.sprk_grantedby is a systemuser lookup (live metadata 2026-09-30); no contact-typed grantor column exists.</existing>
    <extension>The write logic IS extended (the shared CreateGrantAsync core — no second writer). The ROUTES cannot join the /api/v1/external-access group: its scheme is workforce-only and its DelegationRuleFilter requires an OBO RetrievePrincipalAccess, which a contact (not a Dataverse principal, CIAM token not OBO-exchangeable) can never pass; making that admin group dual-scheme would expose every admin mutation to CIAM tokens. The filter is new because DelegationRuleFilter's check is the wrong question for a contact; its shape is copied from it. The lookup is new because sprk_grantedby cannot reference a contact. The column script is new because no script adds a column to sprk_externalrecordaccess (scripts/Deploy-AccessEventEntity.ps1 deploys a different entity); it copies that script's shape. The membership eligibility check EXTENDS QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync rather than adding a reader.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The owner-mandated capability does not exist: a Full Access or Collaborate contact who clicks "Invite User" gets an authentication failure (bff-client.ts:317-322 posts to a route CIAM cannot reach) and, even if it were reachable, /invite writes no grant. Without the contact-typed grantor column a contact-issued grant has no record of who issued it, so "revoke only what you granted" cannot be enforced and the audit trail for an external user minting access is empty.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

