  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A CIAM contact with a Collaborate grant on project P grants a colleague (active member of the grantor's organization) Collaborate: 200, one sprk_externalrecordaccess row for the colleague on P at Collaborate, contact-grantor column = the caller, sprk_grantedby empty, expiry = today + 90 when none was sent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cap: the same Collaborate grantor requesting Full Access writes Collaborate and returns `narrowed = true`; a Full Access grantor requesting Full Access gets Full Access.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">View Only grantor → 403 `sdap.access.contact_grant.level_insufficient`, no write; a caller with no access to the root gets the same response (indistinguishable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A workforce SYSTEMUSER principal calling any new route → 403 `sdap.access.contact_grant.use_manage_access`, no write. This includes a systemuser that ALSO carries a linked contact id (task 141's user↔contact link): the principal kind decides, not the presence of a ContactId. Unauthenticated → 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Organization scope:
- a grantee not an active member of any of the grantor's active organizations → 422 `sdap.access.contact_grant.grantee_not_in_organization`, no write, with twins covering an inactive (statecode 1) membership and an ENDED (`sprk_enddate` past) membership;
- a grantor with no active organization → 403 `sdap.access.contact_grant.no_organization`;
- a membership read fault → 503 `sdap.access.contact_grant.membership_unreadable` with a message, not no_organization;
- self-grant → 400;
- no code path on this route writes `sprk_contactorganization` (asserted: the Dataverse double records no create or update on that entity set).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The request DTO has no organization-grantee member AND rejects unknown members. System.Text.Json IGNORES unknown properties by default, so omitting the member alone would silently accept `organizationId` and ignore it. Mark the DTO `[JsonUnmappedMemberHandling(JsonUnmappedMemberHandling.Disallow)]`, or reject explicitly. A body carrying `organizationId` (with or without a contact) is rejected 400, and nothing is written (asserted end-to-end through the route, not on the DTO type alone).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Restricted root → refused, no write. Because the grantor's own post-veto level there is None, the filter answers 403 `sdap.access.contact_grant.level_insufficient` first. The core's 422 `sdap.access.grant.record_restricted` (task 138) is ALSO asserted by calling the handler's write path with a Restricted flag fixture past the filter, so the core refusal is proven reachable and not just shadowed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Grantee on the record's No Access List (directly or via organization) → 422 `sdap.access.grant.grantee_denied` (task 139's code and entry point), no write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Someone else's access is never changed:
- a grantee holding an active row issued by a systemuser (or by another contact) → 409 `sdap.access.contact_grant.managed_elsewhere`, row unchanged (level, expiry and both grantor columns identical before and after);
- on a row the caller issued: a higher request (within the cap) raises it; a lower request → 409 `sdap.access.grant.would_lower_existing`, row unchanged; an earlier expiry never shortens it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Secure and Limited roots: a contact whose ONLY access is an organization-inherited grant cannot grant (level from direct grants only → none, 403 level_insufficient); a contact with a direct Collaborate grant on the same root can. Asserted for a Secure root AND for a Limited root.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Past expiry → 400 `sdap.access.grant.expiry_in_past`, no write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Ambiguous email (two active org members share it) → 409 `sdap.access.contact_grant.grantee_ambiguous`, no write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Workforce contact-only grantor: granting an existing colleague works; the new-person branch is unreachable (no ProvisionAsync call, asserted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">List: returns only the grants the caller issued on that root; another contact's issued grants are not returned.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Revoke: the caller revokes a grant they issued → row deactivated, 200; a grant issued by someone else or a non-existent id → identical 404 `sdap.access.contact_grant.not_found` (same body shape, so not an access-record oracle); a Dataverse fault → ProblemDetails with a message and reasonCode `sdap.access.contact_grant.revoke_failed` (never a bare 500); a grantor whose own level fell to View Only can no longer revoke (403).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ContactGrantorFilter denies an unmapped request type by default (test with a route bound to an unknown DTO); the new routes are registered as governed in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">/grant and /invite-and-grant behaviour is unchanged by the core extension (their existing suites green without edits for this reason).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">External SPA: "Invite User" is shown for Collaborate and Full Access and hidden for View Only. Asserted by rendering ProjectPage's Contacts tab, not only the `canInvite` helper: ProjectPage.tsx:282 has its own inline check, and InviteUserDialog.tsx:167-170 has a FullAccess-only guard that must also change. The dialog offers only levels ≤ the caller's; no code path in external-spa calls `/api/v1/external-access/*`; `npm run build` and `npm run lint` pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Manage Access shows contact-issued grants with their contact grantor; a systemuser can revoke them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build green; BFF unit + integration + ArchTests green; publish size reported per CLAUDE.md §10 (both absolute sizes, delta, tool, equal file counts) and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">MANUAL LIVE GATE (spaarkedev1, existing test identities incl. a CIAM contact; no user relocation): (a) a CIAM contact with Collaborate on a Standard project invites an existing colleague of their organization at Collaborate from the SPA; the colleague signs in and sees the project; (b) the same contact tries Full Access → Collaborate written, narrowed notice shown; (c) after a Write-holder switches that project to Restricted, the contact no longer sees it in the SPA and a direct API grant call is refused (403 level_insufficient); (d) a View Only contact sees no Invite button and a direct API call is refused; (e) the grantor revokes the colleague's grant from the SPA and the colleague loses the project within the cache TTL; (f) the row shows the contact grantor in Manage Access, and a systemuser revokes a second contact-issued grant from there; (g) inviting a contact of a DIFFERENT organization is refused with the grantee_not_in_organization message; (h) inviting a colleague who already holds a systemuser-issued grant is refused with the managed_elsewhere message and their row is unchanged. Recorded in notes/task-140-contact-side-grant.md.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>New feature required by the owner's C4 answer (session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md round 1 "C4", round 2 item 3, Q1, Q2) and the session 27 C4 research ("Contacts cannot grant at all … needs a new contact-side grant path"). Related defects: C4 (grant model), C1/C2 (plane parity + rights gates, via 135/136), C5 (cache invalidation keyed on the caller's tid: a CIAM grantor invalidates under the CIAM tid, which is right for a CIAM grantee and wrong for a workforce-plane grantee; task 137 (C5) owns that keying, so record the interaction in notes), C7 (task 141, workforce contact identity: why workforce-plane grantors cannot onboard). Open owner questions are escalation triggers 1, 2, 3 and 6 (6 = contacts may not create/alter org memberships; recommended NO and implemented as NO). The external SPA is also the Teams-tab host (ADR-028 A2, one shared standalone-MSAL module), so the SPA wiring covers Teams. Hot-path: BFF Y, SpaarkeAi N, ci-workflows N, skill-directives N, root-CLAUDE.md N.

Review 2026-09-30 (adversarial). Provenance: this file was NOT written by the grant-model author, and was reviewed with that in mind. Deps confirmed as 135, 136, 138, 139 (131 transitively).

Fixes:
- The schema step moved to an operator-run script per the owner's 2026-09-04 directive (AP-13).
- The membership reader was corrected to ExternalParticipationService.QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync, date-bounded and fault-distinguishing.
- The deny, never-lower and ceiling semantics were aligned with task 139's binding codes.
- Proxy revocation/extension via rows issued by someone else is closed (managed_elsewhere).
- The DTO unknown-member 400 was made real (System.Text.Json ignores unknown members by default).
- The Restricted refusal order was made explicit.
- Provenance display was coordinated with 064/066.
- The org-membership owner question was added.</notes>

